## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical design of end-to-end attestation workflows in multi-tenant environments with integrated policy enforcement and security controls.

## Key Concepts
- Post-deployment tenant-scoped attestations using HSM-based key management
- SBOM integrity verification and runtime hashing for supply chain security
- OPA/Gatekeeper integration for policy validation and traffic gating
- Multi-tenant security isolation with compliance enforcement mechanisms

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sample attestation verification pseudocode
function verifyAttestation(attestation, tenantPolicy) {
  // Validate signature with tenant's HSM public key
  const isValidSignature = crypto.verify(
    attestation.signature,
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.publicKey
  );

  // Check policy compliance through OPA/Gatekeeper
  const isCompliant = opa.evaluate(
    attestation.payload,
    tenantPolicy.constraints
  );

  return isValidSignature && isCompliant;
}
```

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of multi-tenant mTLS, dynamic certificate reloading, and sidecar patterns. It tests knowledge of secure-by-default design and how certificate rotation integrates with live production traffic.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant TLS materials and certificate management
- Sidecar dynamic TLS reload mechanisms
- Internal CA API integration and certificate rotation
- Header-based tenant identification (X-TENANT-ID)
- Gateway validation rules and trust models

## Code Example
```go
// Fetch tenant certificate, cache with TTL, and wire into TLS config
func (s *Sidecar) getClientCert(tenantID string) (*tls.Certificate, error) {
    if cert, ok := s.certCache.Get(tenantID); ok {
        return cert, nil
    }
    cert, err := s.caClient.FetchCertificate(tenantID)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }
    s.certCache.Set(tenantID, cert, certTTL)
    return cert, nil
}
```
